getGroupIdsWithViewPermission uses resource UUID instead of group ID

In V2, group permission resources are stored with their name set to the group ID (see getOrCreateResource/resolveGroup, and hasPermission() which does resourceStore.findByName(server, groupId)). Here the callback uses groupResource.getId() (the Resource's persistence UUID), not groupResource.getName() (the group ID).

Two consequences:
1. hasPermission(groupResource.getId(), ...) passes a resource UUID to findByName, which won't match any resource (names are group IDs). It then falls through to the 'all-groups' fallback branch and evaluates against the wrong resource, producing incorrect view-permission results.
2. granted.add(groupResource.getId()) returns resource UUIDs. This set is passed via UserModel.GROUPS to the JPA user query (JpaUserProvider), which expects actual group IDs, so member filtering breaks and no/incorrect users are returned.

Use groupResource.getName() in both places.

Proposed patch:
```diff
--- a/services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/services/resources/admin/permissions/GroupPermissionsV2.java
+++ b/services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/services/resources/admin/permissions/GroupPermissionsV2.java
@@ -123,8 +123,8 @@ class GroupPermissionsV2 extends GroupPermissions {
         Set<String> granted = new HashSet<>();

         resourceStore.findByType(server, AdminPermissionsSchema.GROUPS_RESOURCE_TYPE, groupResource -> {
-            if (hasPermission(groupResource.getId(), AdminPermissionsSchema.VIEW_MEMBERS, AdminPermissionsSchema.MANAGE_MEMBERS)) {
-                granted.add(groupResource.getId());
+            if (hasPermission(groupResource.getName(), AdminPermissionsSchema.VIEW_MEMBERS, AdminPermissionsSchema.MANAGE_MEMBERS)) {
+                granted.add(groupResource.getName());
             }
         });


