After acquiring the write lock, `entryPointAssetsCache = result` is assigned unconditionally even when `err != nil`. If `readWebAssetsFromFile`/`readWebAssetsFromCDN` fails, `result` is nil (or partial), which clobbers any previously cached good value and stores nil into the cache. Subsequent callers then re-enter the slow path every time (cache never hot) and the return value `entryPointAssetsCache` becomes nil. The previous behavior was the same single-assignment, but with locking now centralizing this, it's worth guarding: only update the cache on success.

